<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - Feb 26.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - Feb 26.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the arrival</p>
<p>schedule for major steel scrap cargoes unloading at the South Korean ports of Inchon, Pusan, Masan, Pohang, Kwangyang and Asan, as detailed on Wednesday by South Korean surveyors.</p>
<p>-- INCHON PORT</p>
<p>VESSEL	    TONNES    ETA	 ETD	  BUYER</p>
<p>Vitoradis	 40,883   Feb 27    Mar 8	Dongkuk</p>
<p>Soldropt	  31,012   Feb 27    Mar 15     Inchon</p>
<p>Baltic Trident  55,000   Mar 11	-	  Inchon</p>
<p>-- PUSAN PORT</p>
<p>Cargo	     36,000   Mar 16	-	  Dongkuk</p>
<p>-- MASAN PORT</p>
<p>Transbridge     29,502   Mar 4     Mar 18     Kisco</p>
<p>-- POHANG PORT</p>
<p>Joy Venture     38,500   Feb 26    Mar 15     Kangwon</p>
<p>Pac Duke	  25,000   Early-Mar Mid-Mar    POSCO</p>
<p>Fruition	  30,000   Early-Mar Mid-Mar    POSCO</p>
<p>T.B.N	     30,000   Early-Apr		POSCO</p>
<p>-- KWANGYANG PORT</p>
<p>No vessel calling schedule as yet</p>
<p>-- ASAN PORT</p>
<p>Tilemahos	 31,045   Feb 6     Mar 1	Hanbo</p>
<p>World Argonaut  28,895   Feb 8     Feb 26     Hanbo</p>
<p>Yun Ling	  22,522   Feb 28     -	   Hanbo</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
